24c552fa2ae1d077236e27f94cf60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:06:30Z","email":"samirmardini12@gmail.com","name":"Samir Mardini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T08:06:30Z","email":"samirmardini12@gmail.com","name":"Samir Mardini"},"message":"feat: production-ready ecommerce base (phases 1-6) with observability follow-up\n\nPhase 1: REDIS_URL now treats absent, empty, and whitespace-only values as unused\nwhile still rejecting malformed URLs; startup logs tag configuration, database, and\nlistening phases with durationMs; homepage requests tag the first usable aggregate\nresponse as startupPhase=first_homepage and subsequent ones as warm.\n\nPhase 2: public storefront reads bound Redis cache ops with REDIS_CACHE_TIMEOUT_MS\nand an isolated non-queueing client; optional homepage sections use withDeadline\nand essential sections fall back to StorefrontUnavailable without fabricating\nprices or stock. Request-local CMS memoization prevents duplicate work and never\nleaks authenticated data. The 10s DB_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS bound is documented as\na per-statement limit, not a total aggregate SLA.\n\nPhase 3: checkout gains database-backed, atomically enforced idempotency via a\nnew checkout_requests table scoped by actor+key with request_hash binding. Guest\nand authenticated flows share one transactional path with cart snapshot locking,\nserver-derived prices, coupon FOR UPDATE, atomic stock deduction, and committed-\nonly cache maintenance. Lost responses replay the committed order; conflicting\nreuse returns 409. Frontend preserves keys across retries of the same attempt.\n\nPhase 4: product_variants.is_active plus inventory_version optimistic concurrency\npreserve variant identity across edits, retire removed variants (ON DELETE\nRESTRICT keeps order history), and block stale admin saves after a purchase.\nOrder transitions are explicit and enforced; cancellation restores inventory\nexactly once inside the same transaction; delivered orders are not auto-restocked.\n\nPhase 5: new POST /api/v1/cart/merge endpoint applies accepted lines atomically\nwith per-line stock/variant/quantity validation and explicit rejected list.\ncart_merge_requests PK (user_id, key_hash) scopes idempotency to the signed-in\nuser; frontend guest-cart uses Web Locks + attempt state so lost responses,\nreloads, retries, and simultaneous tabs cannot double-apply.\n\nPhase 6: STORE_* env fields centralize currency, tax, shipping, and locale with\n/api/v1/store/config exposing authoritative settings; EMAIL_MODE=mock is restricted\nto dev/test; production email requires Resend + verified sender; provider failures\nretry with a shared opaque idempotency key and never log recovery tokens or\nmessage content; password recovery returns a generic response immediately with\ndelivery dispatched asynchronously. Checkout quotes include coupons and shipping;\norder creation revalidates and returns QUOTE_CHANGED on drift. Historical orders\nretain their currency via migration 016. Existing COD workflow preserved.\n\nVerification (phase 7):\n- backend 149 offline tests pass; tsc --noEmit clean\n- 58 real-PostgreSQL behavioral subtests pass across checkout, inventory,\n  cart-merge, and checkout-quote suites against a disposable local database\n- frontend 28 unit tests pass; typecheck clean\n- 20 pre-existing admin/auth integration tests still require a local Postgres\n  with user elecshop; outside this scope and unchanged from baseline\n\nRemaining acceptance step: rehearse db:deploy against representative pre-change\nproduction data to confirm migration 014''s FK retarget and 016''s currency\ndefault do not lock-escalate at real volume.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8877336b0d125f940dc11fc32271423d8fad32d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/git/trees/8877336b0d125f940dc11fc32271423d8fad32d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/git/commits/68d74d8b72924c552fa2ae1d077236e27f94cf60","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/211663856?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SamirMD0","id":211663856,"login":"SamirMD0","node_id":"U_kgDODJ278A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/commit/68d74d8b72924c552fa2ae1d077236e27f94cf60","node_id":"C_kwDOSLfdQNoAKDY4ZDc0ZDhiNzI5MjRjNTUyZmEyYWUxZDA3NzIzNmUyN2Y5NGNmNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/commit/6d0d50815c82decb49727a5dc52c3d92920c7aee","sha":"6d0d50815c82decb49727a5dc52c3d92920c7aee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/commits/6d0d50815c82decb49727a5dc52c3d92920c7aee"}],"sha":"68d74d8b72924c552fa2ae1d077236e27f94cf60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/commits/68d74d8b72924c552fa2ae1d077236e27f94cf60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/211663856?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SamirMD0","id":211663856,"login":"SamirMD0","node_id":"U_kgDODJ278A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/commits/6d0d50815c82decb49727a5dc52c3d92920c7aee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T11:28:54Z","email":"samirmardini12@gmail.com","name":"Samir Mardini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T11:28:54Z","email":"samirmardini12@gmail.com","name":"Samir Mardini"},"message":"perf(db): apply base schema once instead of on every start\n\nThe Render Start Command runs on every process start - deploys, crash\nrestarts and free-tier spin-up - so migrate:prod re-executed the whole\n1027-line schema.sql each time. That was safe but wasteful: 50 ALTER TABLE\nstatements each taking a brief ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock, and a DO block that\ndropped and re-added users_role_check on every run, forcing a full\nvalidation scan of users and leaving a window with the constraint absent.\n\nGuard the base schema behind a sentinel row (''000_base_schema'') in the\nexisting schema_migrations ledger. The sentinel is written in the same\ntransaction as schema.sql, so the database moves from \"no base schema\" to\n\"base schema plus sentinel\" atomically - a run that dies part-way rolls\nback both and is correctly seen as uninitialised on the next attempt.\nMigrations still run on every start, which is the part that must.\n\nThe sentinel id sorts before every real migration and matches no migration\nfile, so the ledger runner never touches it. Databases initialised before\nthis change have no sentinel, so they take one final full schema pass to\nrecord it and skip from then on.\n\nSplit the lock budget: waiting on another deployment''s advisory lock now\nallows 180s (a full bootstrap takes ~25s, and the old shared 30s could\ntime out a legitimately queued deploy), while table locks taken during DDL\nkeep the tighter 30s.\n\nVerified on PostgreSQL 18:\n- fresh database: schema + 12 migrations, sentinel written, exit 0\n- restart: \"checking migrations only\", 0 applied, exit 0\n- three concurrent runs on a fresh database: all exit 0, one initialises\n  and two wait then skip; 33 tables, exactly 1 sentinel, 0 duplicate ids\n- schema failure mid-file: exit 1, nothing committed, no sentinel, retry\n  after fixing the cause completes normally\n- users_role_check oid unchanged across restarts (was recreated each run)\n- 116/116 backend tests pass\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4e2fa553e0461bab4723e675dc4da783c31e48c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/git/trees/d4e2fa553e0461bab4723e675dc4da783c31e48c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/git/commits/6d0d50815c82decb49727a5dc52c3d92920c7aee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/211663856?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SamirMD0","id":211663856,"login":"SamirMD0","node_id":"U_kgDODJ278A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/commit/6d0d50815c82decb49727a5dc52c3d92920c7aee","node_id":"C_kwDOSLfdQNoAKDZkMGQ1MDgxNWM4MmRlY2I0OTcyN2E1ZGM1MmMzZDkyOTIwYzdhZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/commit/22e0be4e6f5c4e0e7e2def4b7e09d40f50f08827","sha":"22e0be4e6f5c4e0e7e2def4b7e09d40f50f08827","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/commits/22e0be4e6f5c4e0e7e2def4b7e09d40f50f08827"}],"sha":"6d0d50815c82decb49727a5dc52c3d92920c7aee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/commits/6d0d50815c82decb49727a5dc52c3d92920c7aee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/211663856?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SamirMD0","id":211663856,"login":"SamirMD0","node_id":"U_kgDODJ278A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SamirMD0","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/commits/22e0be4e6f5c4e0e7e2def4b7e09d40f50f08827/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T10:29:56Z","email":"samirmardini12@gmail.com","name":"Samir Mardini"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T10:29:56Z","email":"samirmardini12@gmail.com","name":"Samir Mardini"},"message":"fix(frontend): unblock Vercel build for Next.js 16\n\nThe Vercel deployment failed after a successful compile and typecheck, in\nVercel''s own onBuildComplete hook:\n\n  Error: ENOENT: no such file or directory, open\n  ''/vercel/path0/frontend/.next/next-server.js.nft.json''\n\nTwo contributing issues, both specific to the Vercel build environment:\n\nRemove the stale frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml. It was last updated in June and\nstill pinned next@15.5.19. Vercel''s builder detected it and selected pnpm\n(\"Detected `pnpm-lock.yaml` 9 ... Using pnpm@10.x\") while the install\ncommand actually ran `npm ci`. node-file-trace, which produces the\n.nft.json files the failing hook reads, resolves pnpm''s symlinked\nnode_modules/.pnpm layout differently from npm''s flat tree. Nothing in the\npipeline uses pnpm - CI, both Dockerfiles and Vercel all run `npm ci`.\n\nDisable `output: ''standalone''` on Vercel. Vercel manages `output` through\nits own deployment adapter and does not support standalone. Standalone is\nstill required by the self-hosted and Docker paths, so it stays enabled\nwhenever VERCEL is unset.\n\nVerified a non-Vercel build still emits .next/standalone/server.js, which\nfrontend/Dockerfile copies.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6600a36a058033f6b536bc5887e55b502c81e6dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/git/trees/6600a36a058033f6b536bc5887e55b502c81e6dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SamirMD0/Connect-Shop/git/commits/22e0be4e6f5c4e0e7e2def4b7e09d40f50f08827","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubus